In violation of the provisions of this Law, whoever commits any of the following acts shall be ordered by the competent department of ecological environment of the people's government at or above the county level to make corrections, or shall be ordered to restrict production or suspend production for rectification, and shall be concurrently fined not less than 100,000 yuan but not more than 1,000,000 yuan; if the circumstances are serious, upon approval by the people's government with approval authority, the violator shall be ordered to suspend business or close down:
(1) Discharging atmospheric pollutants without obtaining a pollutant discharge permit according to law;
(2) Discharging atmospheric pollutants in excess of the emission standards for atmospheric pollutants or in excess of the total emission control targets for key atmospheric pollutants;
(3) Discharging atmospheric pollutants by means of evading supervision.

In violation of the provisions of this Law, whoever commits any of the following acts shall be ordered by the competent department of ecological environment of the people's government at or above the county level to make corrections, and shall be fined not less than 20,000 yuan but not more than 200,000 yuan; if refuses to make corrections, the violator shall be ordered to suspend production for rectification:
(1) Encroaching upon, damaging, or without authorization moving or altering atmospheric environmental quality monitoring facilities or automatic monitoring equipment for atmospheric pollutant emissions;
(2) Failing to monitor the industrial waste gases and toxic and hazardous atmospheric pollutants discharged and to preserve the original monitoring records in accordance with the provisions;
(3) Failing to install or use automatic monitoring equipment for atmospheric pollutant emissions in accordance with the provisions, or failing to connect with the monitoring equipment of the competent department of ecological environment and ensure the normal operation of the monitoring equipment in accordance with the provisions;
(4) Key pollutant-discharging units failing to disclose or failing to truthfully disclose automatic monitoring data;
(5) Failing to set up discharge outlets for atmospheric pollutants in accordance with the provisions.

Article 103: Where anyone, in violation of this Law, commits any of the following acts, the market supervision and administrative department of the local people's government at or above the county level shall order rectification, confiscate the raw materials, products, and illegal gains, and concurrently impose a fine of not less than one time but not more than three times the value of the goods:
(1) Selling coal or petroleum coke that does not meet quality standards;
(2) Producing or selling raw materials or products whose volatile organic compound content does not meet quality standards or requirements;
(3) Producing or selling fuels, engine oils, nitrogen oxide reductants, fuel and lubricating oil additives, and other additives for motor vehicles, vessels, and non-road mobile machinery that do not meet standards;
(4) Selling high-pollution fuels within designated no-burning zones.

Article 104: Where anyone, in violation of this Law, commits any of the following acts, the Customs shall order rectification, confiscate the raw materials, products, and illegal gains, and concurrently impose a fine of not less than one time but not more than three times the value of the goods; if the act constitutes smuggling, the Customs shall impose a penalty according to law:
(1) Importing coal or petroleum coke that does not meet quality standards;
(2) Importing raw materials or products whose volatile organic compound content does not meet quality standards or requirements;
(3) Importing fuels, engine oils, nitrogen oxide reductants, fuel and lubricating oil additives, and other additives for motor vehicles, vessels, and non-road mobile machinery that do not meet standards.

Article 108: Where anyone, in violation of this Law, commits any of the following acts, the competent department of ecological environment of the people's government at or above the county level shall order rectification and impose a fine of not less than 20,000 yuan but not more than 200,000 yuan; if the party refuses to rectify, it shall be ordered to suspend production for remediation:
(1) In production or service activities generating waste gases containing volatile organic compounds, the operation is not carried out in a confined space or equipment, pollution prevention facilities are not installed or used as required, or measures to reduce waste gas emissions are not taken;
(2) An industrial painting enterprise fails to use low-volatile organic compound content coatings or fails to establish or maintain records;
(3) An enterprise producing or using organic solvents in the petroleum, chemical or other industries fails to take measures for daily maintenance and repair of pipelines and equipment to reduce material leakage, or fails to promptly collect and dispose of leaked materials;
(4) Oil and gas storage depots, filling stations, tank trucks, etc., fail to install and properly use oil and gas recovery devices as required by relevant state regulations;
(5) Enterprises in iron and steel, building materials, non-ferrous metals, petroleum, chemical, pharmaceutical, mineral mining, etc., fail to take measures such as centralized collection and treatment, confinement, enclosure, covering, cleaning, and sprinkling to control and reduce emissions of dust and gaseous pollutants;
(6) Combustible gases generated in industrial production, landfill, or other activities are not recovered and utilized, are not subjected to pollution prevention treatment when recovery and utilization conditions are not available, or the recovery and utilization device for combustible gases cannot operate normally and is not repaired or updated in a timely manner.

Article 117: Where anyone, in violation of this Law, commits any of the following acts, the competent department of ecological environment and other relevant departments of the people's government at or above the county level shall, within their respective functions, order rectification and impose a fine of not less than 10,000 yuan but not more than 100,000 yuan; if the party refuses to rectify, it shall be ordered to suspend work for remediation or suspend business for remediation:
(1) Failing to confine materials prone to fugitive dust such as coal, coal gangue, coal slag, coal ash, cement, lime, gypsum, and sand;
(2) For materials prone to fugitive dust that cannot be confined, failing to set up tight enclosures not lower than the height of the stacked materials, or failing to take effective covering measures to prevent dust pollution;
(3) Failing to adopt airtight or sprinkling methods to control dust emissions during loading and unloading of materials;
(4) Failing to take anti-ignition measures when storing materials such as coal, coal gangue, coal slag, and coal ash;
(5) Docks, mines, landfills, and disposal sites failing to take effective measures to prevent dust pollution;
(6) Enterprises and institutions that discharge toxic and hazardous air pollutants listed in the Catalogue of Toxic and Hazardous Air Pollutants failing to establish an environmental risk early warning system as required, or failing to conduct regular monitoring of discharge outlets and surrounding environment, investigate environmental safety hazards, and take effective measures to prevent environmental risks;
(7) Enterprises, institutions, other business operators, and operators of waste incineration facilities that discharge persistent organic pollutants into the atmosphere failing to adopt technical methods and processes conducive to reducing emissions of persistent organic pollutants and to install purification devices as required by relevant state regulations;
(8) Failing to take measures to prevent the emission of malodorous gases.

Article 123: Where an enterprise, institution, or other business operator, in violation of this Law, commits any of the following acts, and having been fined and ordered to rectify, refuses to rectify, the administrative organ that made the penalty decision may, in accordance with law, impose a daily recurring fine based on the original fine amount from the day following the date of the order for rectification:
(1) Discharging air pollutants without obtaining a pollutant discharge permit according to law;
(2) Discharging air pollutants exceeding the air pollutant emission standards or exceeding the total emission control targets for key air pollutants;
(3) Discharging air pollutants by means of evading supervision;
(4) Failing to take effective measures to prevent dust pollution during construction or storage of materials prone to fugitive dust.
